    "Lesson_0001": {
      "Name": "Lesson_0001",
      "Number": 1,
      "IndividualizedLessonPassingCriteria": [{
        "AccuracyRequirement": 50.0,
        "SpeedRequirement": 10
      }],
      "Description": "To The Hesitating Purchaser",
      "Lines": [{
        "Line_01": "To The Hesitating Purchaser",
        "Line_02": "If sailor talos to sailor tunes,",
        "Line_03": "Storm and adventure, heat and cold,",
        "Line_04": "If schooners, islands, and maroons",
        "Line_05": "And Buccaneers and buried Gold,",
        "Line_06": "And all the old romance, retold",
        "Line_07": "Exactly in the ancient way,",
        "Line_08": "Can please, as me they pleased of old,",
        "Line_09": "The wiser youngsters of today:",
        "Line_10": "-So be it, and fall on! If no,",
        "Line_11": "If studios youth no longer crave,",
        "Line_12": "His ancient appetites forgot,",
        "Line_13": "Kingston, or Ballantyne the brave,",
        "Line_14": "Or Cooper of the wood and wave:",
        "Line_15": "So be it, also! And may I",
        "Line_16": "And all my pirates share the grave",
        "Line-17": "Where these and their creations lie!"
      }]
    },
    "Lesson_0002": {
      "Name": "Lesson_0002",
      "Number": 2,
      "IndividualizedLessonPassingCriteria": [{
        "AccuracyRequirement": 50.0,
        "SpeedRequirement": 10
      }],
      "Description": "Part 1 - Chapter 1 - Page 1: The Old Sea Dog At the 'Admiral Benbow'",
      "Lines": [{
        "Line_01": "Squire Trelawney, Dr. Livesey, and the rest of these",
        "Line_02": "gentlemen having asked me to write down the whole",
        "Line_03": "particulars about Treasure Island, from the beginning",
        "Line_04": "to the end, keeping nothing back but the bearings of",
        "Line_05": "the island, and that only because there is still treasure",
        "Line_06": "not yet lifted, I take up my pen in the year of grace",
        "Line_07": "17-, and go back to the time when my father kept",
        "Line_08": "the 'Admiral Benbow' inn, and the brown old seaman,",
        "Line_09": "with the sabre cut, first took up his lodging under our roof.",
        "Line_10": "I remember him as if it were yesterday, as he came",
        "Line_11": "plodding to the inn door, his sea-crest following behind",
        "Line_12": "him in a hand-barrow; a tall, strong, heavy, nut-brown",
        "Line_13": "man; his tarry pigtail falling over the shoulders of",
        "Line_14": "his soiled blue coat; his hands ragged and scarred, with"
      }]
    },
